        "comments": "The assembly mCerEla1.hap1.2 is based on 30x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds are named by synteny based on Cervus elaphus (red deer) GCA_910594005.1. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 17 (14.5-17.0 Mbp) is unknown. The chromosomes were named and oriented based on Cervus elaphus (red deer) GCA_910594005.1.",
